{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation landed in the worktree; verification so far.\n\nSplit executed exactly as planned, all five moved regions proven BYTE-IDENTICAL to `origin/main`'s `event_append.py` by substring assertion (PREP 111 lines, GIT1 175, GIT2 14, ORCH 299, RECOV 127 — all True).\n\nSizes: `event_append.py` 794 -> 534 (AC ≤ 560; 266 LOC of cap headroom); `event_prepare.py` 145; `event_commit_git.py` 226. Every `src/rebar/**` file ≤ 800.\n\nLeaf-ness verified by AST import inspection (not raw text — the module docstrings mention the sibling names on purpose):\n- `event_prepare` imports: `__future__`, `os`, `typing`, `rebar._store`, `rebar._store.canonical`, `rebar.reducer._version`.\n- `event_commit_git` imports: `__future__`, `os`, `subprocess`, `time`, `collections.abc`, `rebar._store.gitutil`.\nNeither imports `event_append` nor the other.\n\nAlias-aware re-export completeness (the AC-4 invariant) run over `tests/` + `src/`: aliases discovered = `_ea`, `_store_append`, `_store_event_append`; 20 distinct referenced names; `getattr` succeeds on the imported module for all of them except two PROSE false positives — `event_append.NAME` (a placeholder in this change's own comment) and `event_append.write_lock` (docstring prose in `_store/lock.py` and `inbound_translate.py`). Neither exists on `origin/main`'s module either, so no binding was dropped. `canonical_bytes` — the alias-only binding the reviewer caught via `tests/scripts/graph/conftest.py:95` `_ea.canonical_bytes` — is re-exported and resolves.\n\nRe-exports use the PEP 484 redundant-alias form (`NAME as NAME`), matching the existing `_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S` precedent, so no `# noqa: F401` is needed and mypy treats them as intentional re-exports. `event_append` calls the relocated verbs by BARE NAME, preserving the single-`setattr`-reaches-both-callers property for `_git_add`.\n\nGates green so far: `make lint` (ruff check + format + zizmor + actionlint) clean; `make typecheck` clean (525 files); all 13 runnable `scripts/check_*.py` gates exit 0 including `check_raw_git_writes.py` (the `# raw-git-ok:` markers travelled with their functions) and `check_complexity_baseline.py --check` (active=53 new=0 increased=0 stale=0); the four generators (`gen_adr_index`, `gen_cli_reference`, `gen_env_registry`, `gen_mcp_reference`) produce no diff. `git status` shows only the three `src/rebar/_store/` paths — zero test edits.\n\nFull CI suite (`pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300`) running."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786607507683965001,"uuid":"6373d3d1-0fc9-4a84-ac10-b07294955e0e"}